ggest that the material system is beginning to sprawl. First, students repeatedly ask which source is the real one. Second, the teacher corrects the same explanation in several places. Third, assessment questions rely on language or representations that appear in only one optional branch. Each sign points to a different repair: clarify authority, consolidate duplication or restore alignment. A resource earns its place by doing a job that the shared route needs, not by being good in isolation."
